# Workflow Router

Canon: `AGENTS.md` § Workflow strictness. Detail: `docs/agent-workflows/workflow-strictness.md`.

## Strictness

Classify risk before pipeline. **Full pipeline = Normal + High-risk only.**

| Mode | Contract |
|------|----------|
| Read-only | none — no production edits |
| Tiny | Problem / Change / Validation (3-line) |
| Normal / High-risk | full contract + ICE when implementation |

Auto-upgrade to **High-risk** for: solver, routing, replay, validation, DTO/schema, migrations, artifact contracts, golden loop, plan-run automation.

Pipeline (Normal / High-risk):

```text
problem -> authority -> contract -> plan -> acceptance tests -> small change -> gate
```

Phase order (Normal+): `align -> contract -> slice -> implement -> verify` (`workflow-phases.mdc`). Reject horizontal phase plans unless user explicitly scoped infra-only work.

Authority for architecture/coupling: if `graphify-out/graph.json` exists, **mandatory** `/graphify` query/path/explain before wide grep or multi-module reads (`graphify.mdc`).

For Shapez2 domain work, route to `shapez2-domain.mdc`.

Rules:

- Normal/High-risk: no production edit until problem, goal, non-goals, contract, and acceptance are clear.
- Full contract must name: source of truth, affected layer, forbidden inputs/outputs, validation command, rollback/stop condition.
- Tiny: 3-line contract only; touched-file validation.
- Ops/recovery tasks: route `ops-recovery.mdc` — no product contract required; recovery scope must be explicit.
- Contract change: spec/brief -> acceptance -> tests -> production.
- Regression: failing repro -> fix -> regression gate.
- Refactor: preserve behavior; update tests only when contract shifts.
- Docs-only: no runtime claims.
- One PR-sized purpose; split mixed work.
- Plan execution: closed-world scope; see `.cursor/rules/agent_scope.mdc`.

Tests must assert real contracts. Avoid weak generated tests and implementation trivia.

Never relax tests to force green.

If behavior authority is missing, stop with `BLOCKED:`.

Validation tiers (when, not what): `docs/agent-workflows/validation-routine.md`.

References: `documents/ai/templates/contract-brief.md`, `documents/ai/templates/pr-plan.md`, `documents/knowledge/raw/ai/manuals/testing.md`.
